1
00:06:00,000 --> 00:06:06,000
American Warships is a action, thriller, science
fiction film directed by Thunder Levin.

2
00:12:00,000 --> 00:12:06,000
When an alien force wages war on Earth, only the crew of the USS Iowa
- the last American battleship, stands in their way.

3
00:18:00,000 --> 00:18:06,000
Captain Winston, played by Mario Van Peebles.

4
00:24:00,000 --> 00:24:06,000
General McKraken, played by Carl Weathers.

5
00:30:00,000 --> 00:30:06,000
Lt. Caroline Bradley, played by Johanna Watts.

6
00:36:00,000 --> 00:36:06,000
Dr. Julia Flynn, played by Nikki McCauley.

7
00:42:00,000 --> 00:42:06,000
Lt. Cmdr. Juarez, played by Devin McGee.

8
00:48:00,000 --> 00:48:06,000
Lookout Dunbar, played by Mandela Van Peebles.

9
00:54:00,000 --> 00:54:06,000
American Warships is a 2012 science fiction war film directed
by Thunder Levin and distributed by The Asylum.

10
01:00:00,000 --> 01:00:06,000
It premiered on the Syfy Channel on May 15, 2012.

11
01:06:00,000 --> 01:06:06,000
In the tradition of The Asylum's film catalog, the film is an extremely low-budget
mockbuster of the Hasbro Studios/Universal Pictures film Battleship.

12
01:12:00,000 --> 01:12:06,000
Initially, the film was titled American Battleship, but Universal later involved The Asylum
in a copyright lawsuit over the film due to its resemblance to their film.

13
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
As a result of the controversy, the film's name
was changed to American Warships.

14
01:24:00,000 --> 01:24:06,000
The tone is thought_provoking and intense.
